I just ran into that messed up town level for the second time in one
night.

The shopkeepers hang out in their shops, being peaceful, not caring
if you drop stuff or take it out.  If you try to pay them, the game
says "X is too far away" or somesuch.  Then the game crashes with
a segmentation fault (of the type where the screen doesn't even
clear.  No savefile left, of course).  The first character I had tonight
encountered a peaceful priestess of random alignment in the altar room,
but after wes5-the-archaeologist had been down to the bottom of the
dungeon and back, the priestess was gone.  I managed to run into
the stores, nab all the useful stuff, and run out before the game
could crash on me.  But then I got killed by a mumak.

In the second game, I had just arrived and found tons of junk I had left
lying around in the altar room (which BTW was desecrated, i.e.
shiver runs down your spine), no priest(ess) to be found.
Decided to run to the store to see if anything good were left.
Second I stepped through the door, blammo!  Segmentation fault.

This is really weird and rather annoying.  Has anybody else
had this problem?  I'm playing NH 3.1.  I wouldn't care so much if
it weren't for the fact that my savefiles are lost when this happens.
A lil' weirdness is OK, but not when it destroys a good game.

